WEBVTT

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:20.670
<v Speaker 1>Welcome back to day two of the Magic the Gathering World Championships. I'm here with Toshinori Shigihara, who has just defeated Dirk Babrowski 2 to one in the round one of today's draft pots. Now Toshinori Shahara is the online qualifier from the Magic the Gathering online Tournament. How are you doing? How are you feeling being here in this whole World Championships?</v>

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:25.040
<v Speaker 2>It's really unbelievable. I can't believe I'm actually here at the World Championships.</v>

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:36.180
<v Speaker 1>And when you were playing online, did you, did you have anything that you were particularly shooting for that anything you imagined that it would be like? How does this compare to what you were thinking about the World Championships was gonna be?</v>

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:54.860
<v Speaker 2>Well, it's, it's certainly a different environment for Magic online because when I play that I'm just in my in my house and I'm comfortable and I just can't keep playing match after match after match. And here at the Pro Tour, it's a whole different experience. There's there's lights, there's there's cameras, there's people watching me. It's it's a little, little nerve wracking.</v>

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:56.360
<v Speaker 1>Seems like you're doing pretty well. Also,</v>

00:00:56.430 --> 00:01:01.690
<v Speaker 1>Stan, this is your first time ever traveling. Are you enjoying the traveling experience? Have you gotten to see any of San Francisco?</v>

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:08.950
<v Speaker 2>Well, it's, it's a lot of fun. It's my first trip to America, first trip abroad, so it's very exciting. But man, the jet lag is just murder.</v>

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:26.910
<v Speaker 1>Right. Well, it does. Doing a lot of traveling. I can, I could sympathize now. There was a huge score of Japanese fans here all rooting on Toshinori. And I'm sure there's a lot of fans back on watching online and on Magic the Gathering, you know the the players online. And do you have any advice for them, those people that next year</v>

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:29.680
<v Speaker 1>wanna try and do what you did and qualify online?</v>

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:42.190
<v Speaker 2>Well, I'm just hoping that I can at least have a winning record, not embarrassed myself too badly at my first pro tour. And I just want to thank everyone who's watching here and watching at home, and I hope I don't let you down.</v>

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:48.610
<v Speaker 1>OK, well, congratulations on making it here. It's a great honor. We're happy to have you here and we'll be watching you throughout the tournament.</v>

